# Winning plan: Kabadi Khata (Waste and Energy track)

> One-line pitch: **"India issued 6 lakh fake recycling certificates because nobody can prove who actually collected the plastic. Kabadi Khata lets the kabadiwala prove it with one photo and a voice note, and catches the recyclers who are lying."**

## The user sentence (the organisers asked for this exact thing)
"Raju collects plastic door-to-door in Lajpat Nagar and sells it for cash. Nothing he does is on record, so the 2026 rules are about to cut him out, and brands keep buying certificates for plastic that was never recycled."

## Architecture (every box should appear on screen in the video)
```
Kabadiwala PWA / WhatsApp-style chat (Amplify Hosting)
   │ photo of scale + pile, Hindi voice note, GPS
   ▼
API Gateway → Lambda ──► S3 (photos, audio)
                │
                ▼
     Strands Agent (on Bedrock: Claude or Nova, multimodal)
       tools: read_scale(photo) · classify_material(photo)
              transcribe(audio) [Amazon Transcribe hi-IN]
              check_consistency(voice, photo, gps, time)
              dedupe(photo perceptual hash)
              create_receipt()  ← the only write tool (allowlisted)
                │
                ▼
     DynamoDB: append-only, hash-chained receipts
       (each receipt stores hash(prev_receipt) → tamper-evident)
                │  QR code on every lot
                ▼
     Aggregator / recycler scans QR → custody hand-off entries
                │
                ▼
     Fraud Radar (EventBridge nightly → Step Functions → agent)
       mass balance: recycler's claimed EPR tonnes vs verified inflow
       reused photos, impossible geo/time, capacity × days
                │
                ▼
     Brand / auditor view, with access controlled by Cedar policies
       kabadiwala: own receipts and earnings only
       recycler: its own inflows
       brand: aggregate provenance of the certificates it bought
       auditor: everything plus the flags
```
- **Bounded agent (copies what won with Beacon):** the agent can only call `create_receipt` after the consistency check passes. On a mismatch (voice says 20 kg, scale shows 12), it asks Raju a follow-up question instead of guessing. It never writes certificates.
- **Cedar:** a rarely used AWS open-source tool and a judging plus. Show the policy file for 10 seconds in the video.
- **Honesty slide (the organisers said this "reads as competence"):** a photo can be staged. Mitigations are perceptual-hash dedupe, geo and time plausibility, mass balance (the catch that matters), and random physical audits flagged by risk score.

## Seed data for the demo
- Do real field work Thursday evening or Friday morning: **photograph 1 or 2 real kabadiwalas' scales and piles** (with permission) and record a voice note. Ten seconds of a real kabadiwala in the video beats anything synthetic.
- Synthetic month: 30 kabadiwalas × ~25 days → ~2,000 receipts flowing into 3 recyclers. **Recycler C claims 38× its verified inflow**, mirroring the real CPCB finding. The radar catches it on screen.

